    "post_rendered": "For a positive integer <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" >,</span> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/456f051f0d6a8b0f2745b1cd63a4b26003858880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb912f901cc0dba33ac9d06a90b262b423d9eb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" > be the number of positive divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" > and the sum of positive divisors of <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" >,</span> respectively. let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"8\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" > be positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/5/345300fa5f8eb54db7c74ed7a7e917038e88198a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma(a^n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" > divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/9/359028ab6ba9b81230683a973a1ffa7996803321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma(b^n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" > for all <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/e/0fe9ab25f780bd03ccf6f599fbf4bd046477ca09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" >.</span> Prove that each prime factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/d/01d11a59cc6916c31f4abf3feda43c5f03459fb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" > divides <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/9/0694912313deb7114796839a578f549e39f235f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" >.</span><br>\n<br>\nProposed by MohammadAmin Sharifi",
    "post_canonical": "For a positive integer $n$, let $\\tau(n)$ and $\\sigma(n)$ be the number of positive divisors of $n$ and the sum of positive divisors of $n$, respectively. let $a$ and $b$ be positive integers such that $\\sigma(a^n)$ divides $\\sigma(b^n)$ for all $n\\in \\mathbb{N}$. Prove that each prime factor of $\\tau(a)$ divides $\\tau(b)$.\n\nProposed by MohammadAmin Sharifi",
