    "topic_id": 2815105,
    "poster_id": 577109,
    "post_rendered": "Cyclic quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\"  width=\"57\" height=\"13\" > with circumcenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"12\" > is given. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > is the intersection of diagonals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\"  width=\"27\" height=\"13\" > and <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\"  width=\"29\" height=\"12\" >.</span> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\"  width=\"19\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\"  width=\"16\" height=\"12\" > be the midpoint of the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"13\" > and <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"12\" >,</span> respectively. Suppose that <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" >,</span> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" > be the circumcircle of triangles <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/4/984cc6b7903307691254f8e66fc45da2018a1d58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADP$\"  width=\"43\" height=\"13\" >,</span> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/3/0c33da4d16bf5f54ce503e3c1277199b0ff3b3d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCP$\"  width=\"43\" height=\"12\" > and <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/1/901a51fc605eb6511bdc365013972cc90f068ea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OMN$\"  width=\"50\" height=\"12\" >,</span> respectively. The intersection point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" > and  <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" >,</span> which is not on the arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/5/be5705efbd8cadc9f9e150349d31b4f9cf1a24b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APD$\"  width=\"43\" height=\"13\" > of <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" >,</span> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > and the intersection point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" > and <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" >,</span> which is not on the arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3d7f187fa7b11af4045466cfaf008735488c9ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BPC$\"  width=\"43\" height=\"12\" > of <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" >,</span> is <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" >.</span> Prove that <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b5d354caeace36961406e5400070bbbff052a53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OF=OE$\"  width=\"81\" height=\"12\" >.</span><br>\n<br>\nProposed by Seyed Amirparsa Hosseini Nayeri",
    "post_canonical": "Cyclic quadrilateral $ABCD$ with circumcenter $O$ is given. Point $P$ is the intersection of diagonals $AC$ and $BD$. Let $M$ and $N$ be the midpoint of the sides $AD$ and $BC$, respectively. Suppose that $\\omega_1$, $\\omega_2$ and $\\omega_3$ be the circumcircle of triangles $ADP$, $BCP$ and $OMN$, respectively. The intersection point of $\\omega_1$ and  $\\omega_3$, which is not on the arc $APD$ of $\\omega_1$, is $E$ and the intersection point of $\\omega_2$ and $\\omega_3$, which is not on the arc $BPC$ of $\\omega_2$, is $F$. Prove that $OF=OE$.\n\nProposed by Seyed Amirparsa Hosseini Nayeri",
