    "post_rendered": "Find all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/1/0215a971250926c74a984d4e0154ef92dcf3a15e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C\\in \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" > such that every sequence of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/8/9e82e7b6846e799d3d26bac1d4b4fa3ea51bfb88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_n\\}_{n=1}^{\\infty}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" > which is bounded from below and for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/a/47affecc93688552c8eca8bc13560d52b4cc28a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" > satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/1/881a9dd3055fc16b067bd3c258e6f2891b616a7c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"$$0\\leq a_{n-1}+Ca_n+a_{n+1}&lt;1$$\"  width=\"213\" height=\"17\" >is periodic.<br>\n<br>\nProposed by Navid Safaei",
